1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,667
Meet Notepad Copilot, an AI workspace for support engineers. Bring case evidence,
human guidance, and reusable knowledge into one place.

2
00:00:11,667 --> 00:00:27,375
Support investigations often span notes, screenshots, logs, and separate AI chats.
This workspace keeps evidence beside the conversation, so engineers can carry context
through the case.

3
00:00:27,375 --> 00:00:39,708
Find what matters without leaving the investigation. Search notes and results,
highlight matches, and move between them with familiar browser-style shortcuts.

4
00:00:39,708 --> 00:00:51,500
New information can arrive while an agent is working. Add a condition or follow-up
question directly in the input box, without rebuilding the conversation.

5
00:00:51,500 --> 00:01:08,792
Here, the engineer adds: use read-only checks, and do not restart the service. The
illustrated response includes the new constraint. Steering applies at the next model
request, not by undoing completed actions.

6
00:01:08,792 --> 00:01:21,792
Keep the original questions, accepted additions, and answers in case history. Archive
findings locally or share them through Azure DevOps Wiki, with redaction and human
review.

7
00:01:21,792 --> 00:01:37,000
Built with Python, PySide, and the GitHub Copilot CLI and SDK. This preview features
an English interface. Capture evidence. Guide the work. Reuse the knowledge.
